    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d168">

                <pb facs="0286" n="212" xml:id="pg212"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Adams</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1876.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-11-17"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 17, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I transmit herewith for your information
                    the copy of a note which, on the 15th instant,<anchor n="*" xml:id="d168-f1"/>
                    Sir Frederick Bruce addressed to this department regarding the action of the
                    Canadian authorities in the case of the Fenian prisoners who were concerned in
                    the recent raid against Canada.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis, Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d168-f1" n="*" xml:id="d168-f1-content">
                <p>For enclosure see correspondence with British legation.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
